      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484521392": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T06:57:13.092897+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "We are looking for a Full Stack Engineer to join our dynamic team.\nWe build scalable web applications using React/NodeJS/PostgreSQL. Our core technologies are Next.js and Supabase.\nThe ideal candidate has a strong foundation of backend logic & databases and has production experience.\nYou will be working directly with clients abroad on exciting cutting edge products.\nWho we are\nAZKY Tech Labs is a UK/Dubai based agency that specializes in building AI powered solutions (SaaS, Internal tools etc) for clients around the world. Over the past 5 years, we have worked with more than 100 foreign companies (startups, SMEs and Enterprises) in USA, UK, EU and Australia.\nWho You Are\nYou're a good fit if you have strong foundations and production experience in React/Node/PostgreSQL.\nAvailability : This role is for immediate hiring. It is not suitable for candidates who are currently employed full-time in another role.\nPrimary Interest : You have a strong, demonstrable passion for backend development. Your primary interest must be in server-side logic, APIs, and databases, not just UI development.\nTechnical Foundation : You must have solid experience with React.js, Node.js (ideally building REST APIs, e.g., with Express), Relational Databases (e.g., PostgreSQL or MySQL). You have architected databases from scratch.\nCore Concepts : You have a strong grasp of Data Structures, Algorithms, and Client-Server Architecture.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain web and mobile applications\nWrite clean, maintainable, and efficient code following industry best practices.\nCollaborate with QA, and product teams to deliver robust features.\nOptimize application performance, scalability, and security.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve technical issues across the stack.\nParticipate in code reviews, provide feedback, and ensure code quality.\nStay updated with emerging technologies and frameworks to enhance development efficiency.\nSoft skills\nGood English\nStrong attention to detail\nProactive, independent working style\nStrong communication and teamwork skills\nEffective time management and ability to prioritize tasks\nDesire to learn and grow as a developer\nSalary Range: Competitive\nPerks for you\nQuarterly Performance Bonus- based on performance and client outcomes\nCompany equipment (up to PKR 130k allowance to upgrade workstation)\nLaptop allowance (when you use your own laptop)\nInternet backup\nMedical insurance (dependents and parents included)\nDirect communication with clients and PMs (US, UK, EU) on a regular basis\nPaid time off\nFully remote and open work culture",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484599302": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T06:57:13.092897+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Summary\nWe are looking for a motivated and enthusiastic Junior Software Engineer to join our development team in Karachi. The ideal candidate should have a strong foundation in programming, a willingness to learn new technologies, and the ability to work collaboratively with senior developers to build and maintain high-quality software applications.\nKey Responsibilities\nAssist in designing, developing, testing, and maintaining software applications.\nWrite clean, readable, and maintainable code under the guidance of senior developers.\nIdentify, troubleshoot, and fix basic software bugs and technical issues.\nAssist in developing and integrating APIs and database solutions.\nParticipate in code reviews and follow software development best practices.\nCollaborate with team members to understand project requirements.\nWrite and maintain technical documentation.\nLearn and implement new tools, frameworks, and technologies.\nParticipate in team meetings and Agile/Scrum development activities.\nRequirements\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.\nBasic knowledge of at least one programming language, such as JavaScript, Python, Java, C#, or PHP.\nUnderstanding of object-oriented programming and fundamental data structures.\nBasic knowledge of databases such as MySQL, PostgreSQL, or MongoDB.\nFamiliarity with Git and version control systems.\nBasic understanding of APIs, software testing, and debugging.\nStrong problem-solving and analytical skills.\nGood communication skills and a willingness to learn.\nPreferred Qualifications\nInternship experience or personal software development projects.\nFamiliarity with frameworks such as React, Node.js, Django, .NET, or Spring Boot.\nBasic understanding of web development and responsive design.\nKnowledge of Agile development methodologies.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive salary based on skills and experience.\nMentorship and technical guidance from experienced developers.\nOpportunities for learning and professional growth.\nA collaborative and supportive work environment.\nExposure to real-world software development projects.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485235005": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T06:57:13.092897+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Summary\nDo you want to contribute to the development of reliable business applications and AI powered solutions while progressively building the skills needed to take ownership of features, integrations, and AI agent implementations?\nKUKA's Business Apps team develops and maintains software solutions supporting Backoffice operations across the AMER region. We are looking for a motivated Junior Software Developer to join our team and contribute to the development of modern business applications, AI powered solutions, and intelligent automation.\nThis position is ideal for a recent graduate or someone passionate about software development who is eager to learn, experiment with new technologies, and grow alongside an experienced team. Professional experience is not required. We value curiosity, problem solving skills, initiative, and a strong willingness to learn.\nNOTE: Although this is a remote role, we will only consider those who are within commutable distance of our corporate office in Sterling Heights, MI as there will be some occasional onsite requirements.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop and maintain web applications, APIs, and integrations supporting business processes.\nContribute to AI agent development using the Microsoft Agent Framework (MFA).\nHelp integrate AI capabilities into existing applications and enterprise systems.\nWork with cloud technologies, primarily Microsoft Azure, to build and deploy software solutions.\nCollaborate with experienced developers on software design, testing, code reviews, and continuous improvement.\nExplore new technologies and identify opportunities to use AI and automation to improve business processes.\nRequired Qualifications\nKnowledge of programming fundamentals and object-oriented programming.\nExperience with at least one programming language through academic projects, personal projects, internships, or professional work.\nInterest in web development, APIs, and modern software architectures.\nStrong problem-solving skills and a willingness to learn new technologies.\nGenuine interest in artificial intelligence, particularly AI agents and software development automation.\nGood communication skills and ability to work collaboratively in a team.\nPreferred Qualifications\nFamiliarity with JavaScript, TypeScript, React.js, C#, or ASP.NET Core.\nBasic understanding of REST APIs, SQL databases, and version control tools such as Git.\nExposure to Microsoft Azure or another cloud platform.\nPersonal, academic, or professional projects involving AI, automation, or web applications.\nFamiliarity with AI development tools or agent frameworks is a plus but not required.\nKUKA is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to building an inclusive and diverse workforce. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, age, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state or local laws.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485386769": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T06:57:13.092897+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Role: Python Developer\nLocation : USA Remote\nPosition Type: Fulltime\nMandatory Skills Required: Python · FastAPI · Snowflake · Elasticsearch · Azure · Master Data Management (MDM)\nTHE ROLE\nWe are looking for a Python Developer with 6+ years of experience to design, build, and support backend services and REST APIs for the MDMLite platform. In this role, you will work with Python, FastAPI, Snowflake, Elasticsearch, Docker, and Azure services to develop scalable, secure, and high-performing applications that support Master Data Management (MDM) processes. You will collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver robust solutions for data management, search, validation, and workflow automation.\nWHAT YOU$B!G(BLL DO\nDesign, develop, test, and maintain backend services and REST APIs using Python and FastAPI.\nBuild and enhance Master Data Management (MDM) functionalities and workflows.\nDevelop APIs for search, record retrieval, record creation, and master data operations.\nIntegrate backend applications with Snowflake for data retrieval, validation, and persistence.\nImplement Elasticsearch-based search, indexing, filtering, and record retrieval capabilities.\nDevelop validation frameworks, duplicate detection logic, exception handling, and API response mechanisms.\nImplement authentication and authorization using OAuth 2.0, JWT, or similar security standards.\nContainerize applications using Docker and manage container configurations.\nDeploy and support applications on Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS).\nConfigure API exposure, routing, and governance through Azure API Management (APIM).\nManage secrets and application configurations using Azure Key Vault.\nBuild and maintain CI/CD pipelines for automated testing and deployment.\nTroubleshoot application issues, API failures, deployment challenges, and integration defects.\nWrite unit tests, integration tests, and API test automation.\nCollaborate with frontend developers, QA engineers, architects, and infrastructure teams.\nMaintain technical documentation, API specifications, and deployment guidelines.\nWHAT YOU BRING\nMust Have\n6+ years of backend application development experience.\nStrong programming skills in Python.\nHands-on experience developing REST APIs using FastAPI or similar Python frameworks.\nStrong understanding of SQL and relational database concepts.\nExperience working with Snowflake, including schemas, tables, SQL queries, and data retrieval.\nExperience with Elasticsearch, including index mappings, search APIs, and query optimization.\nStrong understanding of REST principles, JSON, HTTP methods, status codes, and exception handling.\nExperience implementing OAuth 2.0, JWT, or similar authentication and authorization mechanisms.\nHands-on experience with Docker, including image creation, Dockerfiles, and container orchestration concepts.\nExperience deploying and managing applications on Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS).\nExperience working with Azure API Management (APIM).\nExperience managing secrets and configurations using Azure Key Vault.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, and deployment processes.\nExperience with Git, code reviews, debugging, and unit testing.\nStrong problem-solving, communication, and collaboration skills.\nGood to Have\nExperience working with Master Data Management (MDM) platforms.\nHealthcare or pharmaceutical industry experience.\nKnowledge of Azure Managed Identity and Workload Identity.\nExperience with Kubernetes troubleshooting, monitoring, and cloud security best practices.\nExperience implementing fuzzy search, matching algorithms, and duplicate detection frameworks.\nWhat you learn new here :\nOpportunity to work on a modern cloud-native Master Data Management platform.\nExposure to cutting-edge Azure technologies, containerization, and scalable backend architectures.\nCollaborative, innovation-driven environment with opportunities for continuous learning.\nWork alongside experienced architects, engineers, and domain experts.\nStrong focus on career growth, technical excellence, and impactful client engagements.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-03T06:57:13.092897+00:00"
